  m_Name: ArabianGazelle
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::WildTamers.Animals.AnimalData
  id: arabian_gazelle
  displayName: Arabian Gazelle
  styleLabel: Graceful & quick
  description: Gazelles are small, graceful antelopes with slim legs and curved horns.
    They can run very fast and leap high to escape danger. They live in dry plains
    and rocky hills, and eat leaves and grass.
  history: Bedouin hunters followed gazelles with salukis and falcons, and gazelle
    meat was a valued food. Arab poets also praised the gazelle's beauty, often comparing
    lovely eyes to a gazelle's. Today, protected reserves in Saudi Arabia help gazelles
    stay safe.
